        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01SN5fZyr2mT8QgfUfQg2qyV",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: How centralized runtime configuration enables secure credential scoping by treating credentials like any other resolved runtime location.\\ntimestamp: 2024-12-19T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages are authoritative architecture decisions; the synthesis directly follows from their explicit design rationales.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2025-06-19\\n---\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] work together as a unified security and configuration pattern. The credential-scoping model \u2014 injecting the Anthropic API key only into child-process environments, never into the Hub\u0027s own process \u2014 is only *reliably enforceable* because [[runtime-paths]] establishes a single composition point where all runtime configuration is resolved.\\n\\nHere\u0027s the connection: the secrets file itself is one of the runtime locations managed by the single path resolver. Because the resolver is the sole place where paths are discovered and validated at startup, it becomes the natural and only appropriate place to load secrets as well. A local secrets loader reads from that git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at that single point, precisely because everything else flows through there already \u2014 adding credential-injection logic to any other part of the codebase would violate the centralization principle.\\n\\nThis makes the credential-scoping model practical rather than merely aspirational:\\n\\n- The resolver validates that the secrets file exists and is readable *before* spawning any child processes.\\n- Every agent gets its credentials injected from the same validated source, through the same code path.\\n- There\u0027s no temptation to scatter credential-loading logic throughout the codebase \u2014 the same centralization that keeps file paths coherent also keeps secrets managed consistently.\\n- Adding a new agent (like the Query agent) means extending the one resolver to inject credentials into one more child-process environment, not adding new secret-handling code paths in parallel.\\n\\nWithout the single composition point, credential scoping would be fragile: different parts of the codebase might accidentally discover or cache the secret. With it, scoping becomes structural \u2014 credentials are simply another kind of runtime location, resolved once, injected precisely, and kept out of the Hub\u0027s own process memory.\\n\u0022}"
        },
        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EzG3LYmJCKqeksPKMtJfzC",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022index.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022# Wiki Index\\n\\n- [[credential-scoping]] \u2014 How the Ingest agent\u0027s Anthropic API key is scoped to its own child-process environment.\\n- [[runtime-paths]] \u2014 How Grimoire resolves runtime file locations from a single composition point.\\n- [[single-composition-point]] \u2014 How centralized runtime configuration enables secure credential scoping by treating credentials like any other resolved runtime location.\\n- [[write-journal]] \u2014 How the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure.\\n\u0022}"
        },
        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RqnmotcVBMMJ3vwdt97MF1",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022log.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022## [2024-12-19] query | created single-composition-point synthesis\\n\\nCreated [[concepts/single-composition-point]], connecting [[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]], in response to the query: \\\u0022How do our credential-scoping decisions relate to the runtime-path decisions?\\\u0022 The synthesis reveals that the single composition point makes credential scoping practical \u2014 rather than scattering secret-loading logic throughout the codebase, the centralized path resolver becomes the natural place to validate and inject credentials into child processes.\\n\u0022}"
        }
